Source: styledscriptures
Section: python
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Reuben Institute <reubeninstitute@gmail.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2

Package: python3-styledscriptures
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, python3, python3-hebrew, python3-pandas
Description: Classes for Reuben Institute's Psalms and Parashot text
 Text, Psalms, and Parashot classes that present Reuben Institute's
 own typesetting of the Psalms (as poetry) and Parashot (as narrative
 prose), with print-quality typography (curly single/double quotes,
 proper punctuation) — the same text across print, web app, and
 social media video.

Package: styledscriptures-data
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, python3
Description: Reuben Institute's Psalms and Parashot text
 Markdown text and CSV metadata for Reuben Institute's own
 typesetting of the Psalms (as poetry) and Parashot (as narrative
 prose) — the text behind the print booklets, web app, and video
 series.
 .
 Fixed reference data (parashah verse ranges) lives under
 /usr/share/styledscriptures. Editable content (episode tracking,
 psalm/parashah text) lives under /var/lib/styledscriptures and is
 meant to be edited in place (e.g. via MediaStudio); it is
 overwritten on package upgrade, so edits must be committed back to
 the source repo first.

Package: styledscriptures-web
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, python3, python3-flask, python3-styledscriptures, styledscriptures-data, fonts
Description: Web viewer for Reuben Institute's styled scripture text
 Flask app for browsing Reuben Institute's own typesetting of the
 Psalms and Parashot in the browser.
